Key ESG Indicators: Suggests sector-specific and general sustainability metrics, including those aligned with Global Reporting Initiative (GRI), Sustainability Accounting Standards Board (SASB), and Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures (TCFD).
Investor-Oriented Reporting: Addresses growing demand from investors, regulators, and stakeholders for consistent and comparable ESG data.
The guidelines aim to enhance corporate transparency, investor confidence, and sustainable development in Poland while aligning with international ESG best practices.', 'Poland', 'climate', 'in_force', '2021-01-01'::date, 'Poland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/145_12', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'sdg13', 'sdg2', 'sdg7', 'sdg16', 'sdg12', 'disclosure', 'sdg15', 'voluntary', 'poland']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('55a03215-2975-5989-991c-e352dcfc5500', 'Poland Technical Assistnce Project - Promoting Better Corporate Practices', 'Technical Assistnce Project - Promoting Better Corporate Practices and Investor Awareness by Enhancing Environmental, Social and Governance (ESG) Reporting and Developing Investment Opportunities', 'The guidelines aim to help companies listed on the Polish stock exchange enhance their ESG reporting practices. It is a roadmap based on international references such as the NFRD, the Sustainable Finance Disclosure Regulation (SFDR) and the Taxonomy Regulation at the EU level, and the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosure (TCFD) recommendations at the global level.', 'The guidelines aim to help companies listed on the Polish stock exchange enhance their ESG reporting practices. It is a roadmap based on international references such as the NFRD, the Sustainable Finance Disclosure Regulation (SFDR) and the Taxonomy Regulation at the EU level, and the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosure (TCFD) recommendations at the global level.', 'The guidelines aim to help companies listed on the Polish stock exchange enhance their ESG reporting practices. It is a roadmap based on international references such as the NFRD, the Sustainable Finance Disclosure Regulation (SFDR) and the Taxonomy Regulation at the EU level, and the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosure (TCFD) recommendations at the global level.', 'Poland', 'climate', 'in_force', '2021-01-01'::date, 'Poland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/145_17', ARRAY['sdg13', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'poland']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('88982c7e-c704-5b3b-96dc-4bdbbff195d3', 'Poland Polish National Action Plan for the Implementation', 'Polish National Action Plan for the Implementation of the United Nations Guiding Principles on Business and Human Rights 2017-2020', 'Poland’s NAP, was adopted by the Council of Ministers on 29th May 2017. The plan aims to enhance the protection of human rights of individuals and to enable them to seek justice when their rights are violated by business. By describing the government’s actions to promote corporate social responsibility, as well as referring to strategic documents in this area, the NAP demonstrates a deliberate state policy of supporting businesses while stressing the need for human rights.', 'Poland’s NAP, was adopted by the Council of Ministers on 29th May 2017. The plan aims to enhance the protection of human rights of individuals and to enable them to seek justice when their rights are violated by business. By describing the government’s actions to promote corporate social responsibility, as well as referring to strategic documents in this area, the NAP demonstrates a deliberate state policy of supporting businesses while stressing the need for human rights.', 'Poland’s NAP, was adopted by the Council of Ministers on 29th May 2017. The plan aims to enhance the protection of human rights of individuals and to enable them to seek justice when their rights are violated by business. By describing the government’s actions to promote corporate social responsibility, as well as referring to strategic documents in this area, the NAP demonstrates a deliberate state policy of supporting businesses while stressing the need for human rights.', 'Poland', 'climate', 'in_force', '2017-01-01'::date, 'Poland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/145_4', ARRAY['regulations', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'sdg15', 'voluntary', 'poland']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('0023d4b6-d3da-5e01-8b3e-1c9d0c27f6ad', 'Poland Best Practice for GPW Listed Companies', 'Best Practice for GPW Listed Companies 2016', 'This is a code of corporate governance contains a set of corporate governance principles and rules of conduct applicable to the relationships between listed companies and their market environment. Upon the entry into force of the Best Practice 2016, the Exchange will monitor issuers’ compliance with the corporate governance rules with a special emphasis on the quality of explanations published by companies in line with the “comply or explain” approach.', 'This is a code of corporate governance contains a set of corporate governance principles and rules of conduct applicable to the relationships between listed companies and their market environment. Upon the entry into force of the Best Practice 2016, the Exchange will monitor issuers’ compliance with the corporate governance rules with a special emphasis on the quality of explanations published by companies in line with the “comply or explain” approach.', 'This is a code of corporate governance contains a set of corporate governance principles and rules of conduct applicable to the relationships between listed companies and their market environment. Upon the entry into force of the Best Practice 2016, the Exchange will monitor issuers’ compliance with the corporate governance rules with a special emphasis on the quality of explanations published by companies in line with the “comply or explain” approach.', 'Poland', 'governance', 'in_force', '2016-01-01'::date, 'Poland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/145_1', ARRAY['regulations', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'voluntary', 'poland']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('9b50687e-9a05-5743-a215-4d6db06ddd91', 'Poland Warsaw Stock Exchange Rules', 'The Warsaw Stock Exchange Rules', 'The Exchange Rules determine the rules of trading on the regulated market.', 'The Exchange Rules determine the rules of trading on the regulated market.', 'The Exchange Rules determine the rules of trading on the regulated market.', 'Poland', 'governance', 'in_force', '2016-01-01'::date, 'Poland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/145_11', ARRAY['mandatory', 'poland', 'mandatory_regulations', 'disclosure']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('3b435a6c-28a7-5760-a5e4-5806deb700a7', 'Poland Act of December 15, 2016 amending the Accounting', 'Act of December 15, 2016 amending the Accounting Act', 'This amendment to the Accounting Act introduced the requirements and structure provided by the Non-financial Reporting Directive 2014/95/EU. The amendments state that: the report on the activities of the unit should include - as far as is relevant for the assessment of development results and the situation of an individual - at least: 1) The financial key performance indicators related to the activities of the entity; 2) non-financial key performance indicators related to the activities of the entity and information about labor issues and the environment. The statement on non-financial information should include at least: 1) a brief description of the entity''s business model; 2) non-financial key performance indicators related to the activities of the entity; 3) description of the policies applied by the entity in relation to social issues, labor, the environment, human rights and anti-corruption, and a description of the results of applying these policies; 4) a description of due diligence procedures; 5) a description of significant risks associated with the activities of the entity which may have an adverse impact, including risks associated with products of the entity or its relationship with the external environment, including contractors, and a description of the management of those risks.', 'This amendment to the Accounting Act introduced the requirements and structure provided by the Non-financial Reporting Directive 2014/95/EU. The amendments state that: the report on the activities of the unit should include - as far as is relevant for the assessment of development results and the situation of an individual - at least: 1) The financial key performance indicators related to the activities of the entity; 2) non-financial key performance indicators related to the activities of the entity and information about labor issues and the environment. The statement on non-financial information should include at least: 1) a brief description of the entity''s business model; 2) non-financial key performance indicators related to the activities of the entity; 3) description of the policies applied by the entity in relation to social issues, labor, the environment, human rights and anti-corruption, and a description of the results of applying these policies; 4) a description of due diligence procedures; 5) a description of significant risks associated with the activities of the entity which may have an adverse impact, including risks associated with products of the entity or its relationship with the external environment, including contractors, and a description of the management of those risks.', 'This amendment to the Accounting Act introduced the requirements and structure provided by the Non-financial Reporting Directive 2014/95/EU. The amendments state that: the report on the activities of the unit should include - as far as is relevant for the assessment of development results and the situation of an individual - at least: 1) The financial key performance indicators related to the activities of the entity; 2) non-financial key performance indicators related to the activities of the entity and information about labor issues and the environment. The statement on non-financial information should include at least: 1) a brief description of the entity''s business model; 2) non-financial key performance indicators related to the activities of the entity; 3) description of the policies applied by the entity in relation to social issues, labor, the environment, human rights and anti-corruption, and a description of the results of applying these policies; 4) a description of due diligence procedures; 5) a description of significant risks associated with the activities of the entity which may have an adverse impact, including risks associated with products of the entity or its relationship with the external environment, including contractors, and a description of the management of those risks.', 'Poland', 'climate', 'in_force', '2016-01-01'::date, 'Poland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/145_15', ARRAY['regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'poland']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('98b81694-e427-5cdd-b029-a6f65a8bac31', 'Poland Code of Best Practice for WSE Listed Companies', 'Code of Best Practice for WSE Listed Companies, 2012', '“The Code of Best Practice for WSE Listed Companies” aims at enhancing transparency of listed companies, improving quality of communication between companies and investors, and strengthening protection of shareholders’ rights, including those not regulated by legislation, while refraining from imposing a burden on listed companies that may outweigh the benefits resulting from market needs. The Code of Best Practice therefore only addresses those areas where its application may have a positive impact on the market valuation of companies, thus reducing the cost of capital.', '“The Code of Best Practice for WSE Listed Companies” aims at enhancing transparency of listed companies, improving quality of communication between companies and investors, and strengthening protection of shareholders’ rights, including those not regulated by legislation, while refraining from imposing a burden on listed companies that may outweigh the benefits resulting from market needs. The Code of Best Practice therefore only addresses those areas where its application may have a positive impact on the market valuation of companies, thus reducing the cost of capital.', '“The Code of Best Practice for WSE Listed Companies” aims at enhancing transparency of listed companies, improving quality of communication between companies and investors, and strengthening protection of shareholders’ rights, including those not regulated by legislation, while refraining from imposing a burden on listed companies that may outweigh the benefits resulting from market needs. The Code of Best Practice therefore only addresses those areas where its application may have a positive impact on the market valuation of companies, thus reducing the cost of capital.', 'Poland', 'governance', 'in_force', '2012-01-01'::date, 'Poland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/145_9', ARRAY['regulations', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'voluntary', 'poland']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
